{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"AC evidence (Gerrit 1892, landed as 9371328844, LLM-Review +1 + Verified +1, CI run 32219790927 success; 25 direct tests plus 3275 reconciler/interfaces tests green). AC1 at-most-one forward and matching reverse per transition -> every test calls a shared _assert_one_to_one helper that reloads both indexes FROM DISK and checks each reverse key points at a local id whose forward entry names that same key, plus no jira_key bound twice. AC2 bind_confirm stays last-writer-wins with exactly one targeted pop, no sweep/detection/abort -> test_bind_confirm_rebind_drops_only_the_differing_old_reverse_key and test_bind_confirm_rebind_does_not_sweep_an_out_of_band_orphan; the second was ADDED after mutation showed a sweep was indistinguishable in the first fixture, and it pins that an orphan the entry never named SURVIVES a rebind. AC3 stale reverse removal only in the permitted cases -> the two above plus test_unbind_clears_both_indexes_and_sweeps_orphans and test_unbind_of_a_keyless_entry_still_clears_its_reverse_key (the 874a regression: only the sweep can find a reverse key when the forward entry has no jira_key). AC4 immutable numeric-ID re-key instead of retiring -> test_rekey_swaps_both_indexes_and_resets_absence (asserts new key, absence reset to 0, jira_id unchanged, old reverse key gone) plus the facade-level test_facade_rekey_reports_a_move_and_updates_both_indexes returning True with no absence recorded. AC5 legacy no-ID records retain current behavior and facade signatures -> test_missing_numeric_id_reads_as_none_without_rewriting (and asserts the read does not rewrite the file), test_facade_rekey_degrades_to_absence_for_a_legacy_entry_with_no_numeric_id (whose fake client raises if consulted), and the parametrized test_facade_rekey_degrades_to_absence_without_a_usable_client covering both no-client and a client predating get_issue_by_rest. SEAM: note_absent_or_rekey stays on the facade as coordinator keeping the guard, the no-client/no-id fall-through and the by-id lookup; only the re-key mutation moved to BindingLifecycle.rekey, which declines on an empty or unchanged current key so both former note_absent branches collapse to one fall-through with NO outcome change. binding_store.py 710 -> 646 LOC; binding_lifecycle.py 229. _env_int and the RECONCILER_ABSENT_RETIRE_GRACE read deliberately did NOT move (they serve note_absent, which is T2 scope), and the implementer kept the non-literal env read on line 109 exactly so docs/env-vars.md stayed fresh. 6 defect-seeded mutations all RED."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787119913528765001,"uuid":"13140549-1ca5-4418-abc9-b1b073a4f632"}